Edge: user submits, request pending, user clicks reset (new submitId), then submits new draft? Button is disabled, so can't. OK.

But wait — there's another subtle issue: after reset during pending, the notice is cleared by reset handler. Then stale result arrives and sets a notice — the notice appears next to the new draft. Requirement says the notice must clearly state it belongs to the pre-reset submission, which we do.

Also "即使用户在同一次等待中多次清空重填，最终保留的也应是当前这一份内容" — generation check handles it.

Also "直接使用'清空重填'且没有请求等待时，仍照常清空内容和提示" — existing behavior.

Now also check: on stale success, should we still regenerate submitId? No — the current draft's submitId must stay so its first submit is independent... actually the current draft's submitId was generated at reset; keep it.

One more: on stale success, we call loadTickets(). Good.

Also the finally re-enables button — but what if... only one request in flight at a time, fine.

